{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-index-top", "R-index-top-in", "L-middle-home"],
  "note": "T2: {Lp-top,Li-top,Ri-top-in,Rp-top} -> {F,G,W,Z} (unordered) => these 4 keys are a permutation of {F,G,W,Z}. Rotated after T2: {L-index-bottom,L-index-top-in,L-ring-home}. T3 press {Lp-top,Li-top,Ri-top-in,L-middle-home}. From T3 obs: identify which 3 of {F,G,W,Z} are on {Lp-top,Li-top,Ri-top-in} plus letter on L-middle-home. Then T4 planned: {Lp-top,Li-top,Rp-top,L-middle-home} to resolve remaining key among {Ri-top-in,Rp-top}."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-pinky-top",
    "R-index-top-in",
    "R-pinky-top",
    "L-middle-home"
  ],
  "locks": {
    "L-middle-home": "J",
    "R-pinky-top": "Z",
    "R-index-top-in": "W"
  },
  "note": "Known now: L-middle-home=J; R-pinky-top=Z; {L-pinky-top,L-index-top,R-index-top-in}={F,G,W} and turn4 implied R-index-top-in=W => L-pinky-top/L-index-top are {F,G}. Next T5 presses {L-pinky-top,R-index-top-in,R-pinky-top,L-middle-home} => output {J,Z,W,(F or G)} gives L-pinky-top; then L-index-top is the other."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-index-top-in",
    "R-index-bottom-in",
    "L-middle-home",
    "L-index-home-in"
  ],
  "note": "T7: pressed {L-index-top-in,R-index-home,R-index-top-in,L-middle-home}->{C,J,S,X}. So L-index-top-in & R-index-home = {S,X} (order unknown). Rot after T7: {L-index-bottom-in,R-index-top-in} rotated => swap (2-key), so after rotation start next: R-index-bottom-in=C; R-index-top-in≠C. L-middle-home stays J. Plan T8 press {L-index-top-in,R-index-bottom-in,L-middle-home,L-index-home-in} to fix whether L-index-top-in=S or X."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-index-bottom-in", "L-index-top-in", "R-index-home", "L-middle-home"],
  "locks": {
    "L-index-top-in": "S",
    "R-index-home": "X",
    "L-middle-home": "J",
    "R-index-top": "C"
  },
  "note": "After T8: L-index-top-in=S; L-middle-home=J; R-index-home=X; R-index-top=C. Also {R-index-bottom-in, L-index-home-in}={H,K}. Plan T9 press {R-index-bottom-in,L-index-top-in,R-index-home,L-middle-home} to get exact letter on R-index-bottom-in; then L-index-home-in is the other."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-top", "R-index-top", "L-middle-home", "R-index-home"],
  "note": "T10 chord {L-ring-top,R-index-top,L-middle-home,R-index-home}. Known: L-middle-home=J, R-index-home=X. After T9 swap: L-ring-top=C. So expect set {C,J,X,?} giving current R-index-top=?. If rotation notice affects any of these, update swap mapping."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-top", "R-index-top", "L-middle-home", "R-index-home"],
  "locks": {
    "L-ring-top": "C",
    "R-index-top": "D",
    "L-middle-home": "J",
    "R-index-home": "X"
  },
  "note": "T10: rotation none. From set {C,D,J,X} on {L-ring-top,R-index-top,L-middle-home,R-index-home} => L-middle-home=J, R-index-home=X, L-ring-top=C, R-index-top=D. Next: chord use known L-ring-top(C)+R-index-top(D) + two unknowns, e.g. [L-pinky-top, L-ring-top, R-ring-home, R-index-top]."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-pinky-top",
    "L-ring-top",
    "R-index-top",
    "R-index-home"
  ],
  "note": "Prev: {L-pinky-top,R-ring-home}={F,W} (C on L-ring-top, D on R-index-top, none rotated T12). T13 press [L-pinky-top,L-ring-top,R-index-top,R-index-home]; with no rotation among these 4, set={C,D,X,?} so ?=L-pinky-top letter. Use rotation notice to adjust if any of these 4 are rotated."
}
